## Docker

A multi-stage `Dockerfile` and `docker-compose.yml` are included. The image
builds a wheel of the project in a builder stage and installs it into a
slim runtime image{% if include_playwright %} together with the Playwright chromium browser and
its system dependencies{% endif %}.

```bash
# Build the image
docker compose build

# Run the CLI inside the container
docker compose run --rm scraper {{ project_slug }} targets
docker compose run --rm scraper {{ project_slug }} run example

{% if include_api %}
# Serve the FastAPI app on :8000
docker compose up api

{% endif %}
# Bring up the optional Postgres backend (uses the `postgres` profile)
docker compose --profile postgres up -d postgres
```

`./data` is volume-mounted into `/app/data` so JSONL files and SQLite
databases survive container restarts. Secrets / connection strings are
read from `.env`.

{% endif %}
## Configuration

Settings are layered with the following precedence (highest wins):

1. Constructor kwargs at runtime
2. Environment variables (and `.env`)
3. `config.yaml` (or JSON) referenced by `CONFIG_FILE`
4. Defaults defined on the pydantic models

Nested keys in env vars use `__`:

```bash
SCRAPER__USER_AGENT="my-bot/1.0"
{% if include_api -%}
API__PORT=9000
{% endif -%}
```

See `src/{{ package_name }}/settings.py` for the full schema.

